jank-20: a native entry per typed arity; native returns, if and loop results; n-ary inline arithmetic
(cohost doc/upstream/jank-20-native-returns.md; lane U6, order U6-1)

Base: jank-lang/jank f3d82d65499920f81216e9235bd5d3a34a968e3f with the series before it in
upstream/jank/patches/series (11, 13, 14, 12-21, 18, 19). Apply from the clone's root: git apply <this file>.

Files:
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/analyze/processor.cpp:
  - analyze_fn_arity: an arity of a fn with no variadic arity, whose typed parameters are all
    native numbers (long, long long, double), gets a native entry when something asks for one: a
    :rettag (defn puts the name's :tag there) that names a native number, or a parameter hinted as
    one. The return type is the hint, or inferred: the body is analyzed assuming i64 (named
    self-recursion typed with it, tail unboxed); if the tail is a native integer, kept; if it is a
    native real, analyzed again assuming that real; anything else (an object tail, a fn-level recur,
    an error under the assumption) analyzes the body again exactly as before (boxed).
  - analyze_fn: :rettag read; native entries only when no arity is variadic.
  - analyze_call: named recursion into the arity being analyzed, when it has a native entry,
    converts its arguments to the parameter types and is typed with the native return type.
  - analyze_if: a branch that ends in recur yields no value, so the if takes the other branch's
    type when it is a native number (a loop carrying native locals keeps a native result).
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/codegen/cpp_processor.cpp: an arity with a native return type is
  emitted as <name>_<n>_native (typed parameters taken natively, native return) plus the boxing
  entry <name>_<n> every dynamic caller uses (unboxes the typed arguments, calls the native entry,
  boxes the result); named recursion into it calls the native entry directly.
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/ir/{builder,instruction,processor}.cpp, include .../ir/*.hpp,
  analyze/expr/{function,named_recursion}.hpp, named_recursion.cpp: the native types carried from
  the analyzer to codegen.
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/analyze/cpp_util.cpp, .hpp: is_native_number.
- compiler+runtime/include/cpp/jank/runtime/convert/builtin.hpp: convert<integral>/convert<floating>
  into_object/from_object always_inline (the boxing entry's unboxing was two out-of-line calls).
- compiler+runtime/include/cpp/jank/runtime/core.hpp: not_(bool) for exactly bool, so (not (< a b))
  stays native; (not 0) still goes through the object overload (false).
- compiler+runtime/src/jank/clojure/core.jank: + - * / inline every arity 2-8, folded left as the
  variadic arity folds (Clojure's nary-inline); before, (* a b c) was a dynamic var call.

